::  What every ship that installs this desk sees in Landscape.
::
::  It says Grubbery, not Lattice, and that is the point of this release. The
::  desk used to be lattice and nothing else, so pointing the tile straight at
::  /apps/lattice was honest. It stops being honest the moment lattice installs
::  itself as a desk from a repo and stands beside other apps: the thing a user
::  installs here is the launcher, and lattice is one of the things inside it.
::
::  site is /apps/grubbery, the shell's own binding — the home surface where a
::  user consents to an app's roads and adds another publisher's desks. A tile
::  pointing at /apps/lattice would 404 on a fresh install, because lattice has
::  no instance until its desk is provisioned and its roads are granted.
::
::  Anyone who installed something called Lattice will find something called
::  Grubbery with Lattice inside it. Worth saying plainly here rather than
::  leaving them to discover it.
:~
  title+'Grubbery'
  info+'The launcher and the apps inside it. Ships with Lattice: pages, a private knowledge store, and MCP memory for AI agents.'
  color+0x8b.4513
  image+'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/gwbtc/grubbery/39a144c/grub.png'
  base+'grubbery'
  site+/apps/grubbery
  version+[1 1 0]
  website+'https://github.com/nisfeb/lattice'
  license+'MIT'
==
